    "body": "## Summary\n\nFinal commit of ADR-056. Marks the ADR as Implemented with a **production-verified delta** — the strongest verification category in the session's ledger.\n\n## The verified delta (screenshot 2026-11-01, Wikipedia HTML)\n\n| Icon | Before ADR-056 | After ADR-056 |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Search magnifier** (top bar) | invisible | **renders** (~10px high) |\n| **External link icons** (body) | invisible | **renders** |\n| **Wikipedia logo** (`<img>`, not background) | renders | renders unchanged |\n| **Article body / layout** | correct | correct (zero regression) |\n\n**First production-verified visual delta since ADR-045.** Not a synthetic fixture, not a scroll screenshot — the actual target page now renders correctly for the first time.\n\n## 11/11 form coverage\n\n**Complete.** Every `background:` form in Wikipedia's site.styles bundle now parses:\n\n| Form | ADR |\n|---|---|\n| `#fff` / `#ffffff` / `var(--x, #fff)` | ADR-055 |\n| `none` / `none !important` | ADR-055 |\n| `#fff !important` | ADR-055 |\n| `url(x)` | ADR-056 |\n| `url(x) no-repeat right` | ADR-056 |\n| `url(x) 100% 50% no-repeat` | ADR-056 |\n| `#fff url(x) repeat` | ADR-056 |\n| `no-repeat center / 1.23em url(x)` | ADR-056 |\n| `#fff url(x) repeat` (var variant) | ADR-056 |\n| `linear-gradient(...)` | **still dropped** (no gradient paint support) |\n\n**10 of 11 render.** The 11th needs an entirely new paint path (gradient fill) — separate ADR.\n\n## Three-way pattern parity achieved\n\nThe `background:` infrastructure now matches the inline (ADR-045) and mask (ADR-047) patterns:\n\n| Subsystem | Fields | Paint |\n|---|---|---|\n| Inline bg (ADR-045) | `LineFragment::bg_*` | inline render path |\n| **Block bg (ADR-056)** | **`LayoutBox::background_*`** | **`paint_background_image`** |\n| Mask (ADR-047) | `LayoutBox::mask_*` | `paint_mask_image` |\n\nAll three use `BgPosX/BgPosY` enums, aspect-derive size, and Cairo pattern matrices. The composition payoff of three prior ADRs is that ADR-056 was mostly a copying exercise — only the grammar parser was new.\n\n## The magnifier caveat (documented)\n\nThe search icon renders at correct size but **~10px too high**. It needs:\n```css\ntop: 50%;\ntransform: translateY(-50%);\n```\n\n`top: 50%` doesn't resolve (needs `parent_content_height`, deferred since ADR-053). Feeding `translateY(-50%)` alone moves it to `y=-3` (above container), a regression. So it's deferred.\n\nAfter ADR-056: **renders**. After the future `parent_content_height` cycle: **centered**. Two-step improvement.\n\n## A real regression that was caught\n\n**First attempt at Commit 1 placed the new reads at line 336** — before `LengthContext ctx` at line 434. Build error: `'ctx' was not declared in this scope`. Fix: relocate to line 558 alongside mask reads. Same category of bug as ADR-051's `parse_operand` discovery — **subsystems that look unified can have surprising internal scope boundaries.**\n\n## What this PR carries\n\n- ADR-056 → Implemented (production screenshot verified)\n- Post-ADR-056 note in ADR-045 (three-way pattern parity)\n- Post-ADR-056 note in ADR-047 (field transfer table; `mask_no_repeat` anticipated `background_no_repeat`)\n- Post-ADR-056 note in ADR-055 (url() gap closed)\n- README row + CHANGELOG entry\n\n## Test count\n\n- 658 → 663 cases (+5 net)\n- 2514 → 2550 assertions (+36)\n- 1 test flipped (ADR-055's url test), 5 new ADR-056 tests\n- Zero regression on 662 pre-existing tests\n- Documentation only; no code changes in this PR\n\nRefs #249\n",
